Vellum patch to RmlUi's default FreeType font engine, against the pinned
58c751531f4c1a1eb2dc56f409b8e8a323a0c9ad. Not an upstream commit: upstream
master (bc6ea0e at the time of writing) has the same code. Candidate for
upstream; any issue or pull request there must be written by a person, per
RmlUi's contribution policy.

The engine summed whole-pixel glyph advances (horiAdvance >> 6) and grid-fitted,
floored kerning, so rounding built up along a string: measured against
CoreText's fractional layout, text came out up to 5 % wider at 10-14 px (Arial
10 px +5.0 %, Verdana 11 px +3.5 %). Each glyph now also carries its unhinted
advance in 26.6 fixed point, kerning is read unfitted in 26.6, and string
width and glyph placement accumulate a 26.6 pen that is rounded once per
glyph position. Glyphs stay on whole pixels. Letter spacing joins the pen
rounded to 1/64 pixel instead of truncated to a whole pixel.

diff --git a/Include/RmlUi/Core/FontGlyph.h b/Include/RmlUi/Core/FontGlyph.h
index b1dc7d6..caf60a9 100644
--- a/Include/RmlUi/Core/FontGlyph.h
+++ b/Include/RmlUi/Core/FontGlyph.h
@@ -45,6 +45,9 @@ public:
 	Vector2i bearing;
 	/// The glyph's advance; this is how far the cursor will be moved along after rendering this character.
 	int advance = 0;
+	/// The same advance in 26.6 fixed point (1/64 pixel), unhinted. The default font engine accumulates these along a
+	/// string and rounds only the pen position, so per-glyph rounding does not build up.
+	int advance_26_6 = 0;
 
 	/// Bitmap data defining this glyph. The dimensions and format of the data is given below. This will be nullptr if the glyph has no bitmap data.
 	const byte* bitmap_data = nullptr;
@@ -61,6 +64,7 @@ public:
 		FontGlyph glyph;
 		glyph.bearing = bearing;
 		glyph.advance = advance;
+		glyph.advance_26_6 = advance_26_6;
 		glyph.bitmap_data = bitmap_data;
 		glyph.bitmap_dimensions = bitmap_dimensions;
 		glyph.color_format = color_format;
